 "inference": [
  "Stomach and limb damage uses the one-value array of the cell, not the scalar: 0.84 for assault rifle, carbine, SMG, PDW and machine gun bullets, 0.91 for DMR bullets, 0.67 for bolt-action bullets, 1.0 for sidearm and shotgun bullets. These are EA's new figures and its stated exceptions.",
  "The head table shared by every bullet holds both EA's old headshot values (1.34, 1.5, 1.75) and the new automatic ones (1.4, 1.57, 1.8); a weapon picks one by index.",
  "The scalar Field_674633de of the same cells still holds the pre-1.3.3.0 values (1.0, sniper 0.8, head 1.34 / 1.5 / 1.75). For soldier body parts it is therefore not the value in use where an array is present.",
  "This matters for earlier leads that multiplied by the scalar for a soldier's abdomen (L3329, L3338, L3342, L3357): each needs its array checked. For vehicle targets the scalar reproduced EA's figures (L3323), so that rule is not affected.",
  "PD_.416Barrett (material 784) holds 1.0 for both, not the sniper 0.67; WEAPONS.md already records its limb value moving to 1.0 in 1.4.3.0."
 ],
